      {
        "id": 88625,
        "name": "Envisioner",
        "username": "Envisioner",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/e/9de053/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2014-02-18T16:50:57.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Foote\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/foote/48/1877_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Foote:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>You think those names were just randomly chosen out of Christophers beard without any consideration to speaking to broader themes?</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I think that if you have two ravens there really isn't anything else you could name then besides \"Bobby\" and \"Steve\" or something comparably dumb.&nbsp; Lilian probably named them herself.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>You guys are so litteral sometimes it drives me nuts.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>It's hard enough to communicate even IF people say exactly what they mean.&nbsp; I don't always succeed in doing so, but if I can't manage to make a clear and explicit statement of precisely what I meant, then I really have nobody but myself (or \"all of you idiots\", but that's me being an arrogant bastard so I try to avoid it) for the fact that nobody understood me.&nbsp; If you mean to say there's a connection with a vaguely Odin-like being, perhaps you should say that, not \"there's a connection with Odin\".</p>",
        "post_number": 30,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:13:21.069Z",
